SUMMARY:Deadline 16:00 CET: Mondriaan Fund: Call for Proposals\, Dutch Pavi
 lion at the Venice Biennale Arte 2028 (EUR 500\,000 presentation budget)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 16:00 CET.\n\nThe first open call for the
  Dutch entry to the Venice Biennale Arte since 2018\, run by the Mondriaan
  Fund for the Ministry of Education\, Culture and Science. ELIGIBILITY: te
 ams of at least one curator and one artist embedded in the Netherlands or 
 Caribbean-Kingdom contemporary art sector\; non-Dutch members are allowed.
 \n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund\nLocation: Venice\, Italy. Teams embedded
  in the Dutch or Caribbean-Kingdom contemporary art sector.\nAward: EUR 50
 0\,000 (incl. VAT\, excl. fees) presentation budget for the selected team\
 ; up to 4 shortlisted teams receive EUR 5\,000 each to develop their plan.
 \nDuration: March 2027 to November 2028\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfond
 s.nl/en/call-for-the-dutch-pavilion-venice-biennale-2028/?utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/call-for-the-dutch-pavilion-venice-bie
 nnale-2028/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Venice\, Italy. Teams embedded in the Dutch or Caribbean-Kingdom c
 ontemporary art sector.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kunstpunt-groningen-tschumi-pavilion-hellend-vlak-2027@artificialnouvea
 u.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261111T133426Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261104
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261105
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kunstpunt Groningen: Open Call Tschumi Pavilion (Hellend 
 Vlak 2027)
DESCRIPTION:Kunstpunt Groningen invites artists to propose a temporary\, si
 te-specific artwork for the Tschumi Pavilion on Hereplein\, Groningen\, vi
 ewable from outside\, that responds to current social and often polarised 
 issues. The brief asks how art can encourage us to look at today's social 
 issues in a different light.\n\nOrganisation: Kunstpunt Groningen\nLocatio
 n: Tschumi Pavilion\, Hereplein\, Groningen\, Netherlands. Applicants must
  currently work in the city or province of Groningen or have a demonstrabl
 e connection to it.\nAward: Up to three shortlisted artists receive EUR 1\
 ,500 (excl. VAT) each for a preliminary design\; the selected artist recei
 ves a EUR 17\,000 project budget\, including their fee. No application fee
 .\nDuration: Commission\; work on display 3 to 4 months (June to September
  2027)\n\nMore: https://www.kunstpuntgroningen.nl/en/tschumi-pavilion/open
 -call-tschumi-pavilion/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.kunstpuntgroningen.nl/en/tschumi-pavilion/open-call-tschumi
 -pavilion/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Tschumi Pavilion\, Hereplein\, Groningen\, Netherlands. Applicants
  must currently work in the city or province of Groningen or have a demons
 trable connection to it.
END:VEVENT
